>Another question about taming scroll, I had a blessed one, and try it on a 
>black dragon, it didn't work. What's the chance of a taming scroll working on 
>something as powerful as that?  It was level 16 I think.
>
The formula for a monster resisting taming is:
   rn2(100) < magic resistance + monster level - LEV

For spells I think LEV is your level, for scroll of taming it's 6.  A black
dragon has a magic resistance of 20, and are normally level 15.  So if
rn2(100) < 20+15-6=29 it will resist.  In other words, you had an over
70% chance of taming it - just bad luck I guess.  An Archon (level 19, 
magic resistance 80) would have been much tougher.
